ithub.com/users/daniel-garcia/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/e81a4180c90502d4d02a7e74d250d66f88425f56/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-05T03:20:55Z","email":"dgarcia@infoblox.com","name":"Daniel García"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-05T03:20:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Issue sweep: DNS UDP (verify), daemon version-skew, Postgres compose isolation, SLO gate + auto-gen, docs drift check, bootstrap skill (#65)\n\n* feat(compose): generate a real Postgres host with per-module schema isolation\n\nde compose build now branches the generated dialector on database.engine: a\npostgres:// / postgresql:// DSN (read from the declared dsnRef env var, not a\nhardcoded <NAME>_DSN) uses the Postgres driver, and gorm.io/driver/postgres is\nadded to the generated go.mod; an empty DSN still falls back to in-memory SQLite\nso the composed binary runs out of the box in dev.\n\nEach module''s migration is scoped to its own namespace: models are routed by the\nmodule''s descriptor ID (matching servicekit''s per-module MigrationRunner call)\ninstead of AutoMigrating the union of every member''s Models() into every schema,\nso schema-preferred isolation actually isolates. The build note now warns only\nfor engines that are still ungenerated.\n\nFixes #64\n\n* feat(daemon): report daemon build version and detect version skew on start\n\nThe daemon now reports its build (version + commit) on GET /v1/status, so\nde status shows it. de start compares the running daemon''s build against this\nclient and, on skew (the client was upgraded but the daemon keeps running the\nold binary), replaces it with stop + start; --no-replace only warns. A daemon\ntoo old to report a version is treated as skew. de project up prints a\nbest-effort skew warning before registering routes.\n\nThis kills the recurring \"route clobber\": a stale daemon that predates a\nrouting change silently mis-registers routes (drops Path) with no other signal.\n\nFixes #56\n\n* feat(slo): add lint --fail-on-warn and auto-generate the OpenAPI when missing\n\nde slo lint --fail-on-warn (alias --strict) exits non-zero on ANY finding,\nincluding warnings, so a production CI gate can fail on un-calibrated or\nplaceholder-policy SLOs; default de slo lint still exits 0 on a fresh scaffold.\n\nde slo generate now runs de generate automatically when the enriched OpenAPI is\nmissing but the project can produce it (buf config present) — the fresh-scaffold\npath that previously errored with \"no openapi/*.openapi.yaml\". --no-generate\nopts out and fails loud with the actionable hint.\n\nFixes #61\nFixes #62\n\n* ci(docs): regenerate CLI reference pages and add a drift check\n\nAdd a docs-cli-check make target that regenerates the CLI reference pages and\nfails if they are stale versus the de command set, and run it in CI so the\nreference docs cannot silently fall behind new commands or flags. Regenerate all\nreference/cli pages wholesale (refreshes slo/start for the new flags).\n\nFixes #44\n\n* feat(skills): ship a discoverable new-service Claude Code skill for greenfield bootstrap\n\nAdd .claude/skills/new-service/SKILL.md: a consumer-facing skill that triggers on\n\"build a <X> service with devedge\" and drives the working flow — pin the SDK\nversion (never @latest), scaffold with de new service, model the resource,\ngenerate, build, run, and round-trip over HTTP. Add a \"Use with Claude Code\"\ngetting-started page (with a card link) and a root AGENTS.md pointer so the path\nis discoverable. In-repo skill + docs ship with no external credentials;\nmarketplace/plugin packaging is noted as a follow-up.\n\nFixes #14\n\n* docs(changelog): record the v0.15.0 issue sweep (#6 #14 #44 #56 #61 #62 #64)","tree":{"sha":"4a050742ccb46a9a8c7a317ba4282875f81f644a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/trees/4a050742ccb46a9a8c7a317ba4282875f81f644a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/commits/e81a4180c90502d4d02a7e74d250d66f88425f56","verification":{"payload":"tree 4a050742ccb46a9a8c7a317ba4282875f81f644a\nparent 41801ff6908fcc0046ae56ed73c5a2b4ae1f9ea9\nauthor Daniel García <dgarcia@infoblox.com> 1783221655 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783221655 -0500\n\nIssue sweep: DNS UDP (verify), daemon version-skew, Postgres compose isolation, SLO gate + auto-gen, docs drift check, bootstrap skill (#65)\n\n* feat(compose): generate a real Postgres host with per-module schema isolation\n\nde compose build now branches the generated dialector on database.engine: a\npostgres:// / postgresql:// DSN (read from the declared dsnRef env var, not a\nhardcoded <NAME>_DSN) uses the Postgres driver, and gorm.io/driver/postgres is\nadded to the generated go.mod; an empty DSN still falls back to in-memory SQLite\nso the composed binary runs out of the box in dev.\n\nEach module''s migration is scoped to its own namespace: models are routed by the\nmodule''s descriptor ID (matching servicekit''s per-module MigrationRunner call)\ninstead of AutoMigrating the union of every member''s Models() into every schema,\nso schema-preferred isolation actually isolates. The build note now warns only\nfor engines that are still ungenerated.\n\nFixes #64\n\n* feat(daemon): report daemon build version and detect version skew on start\n\nThe daemon now reports its build (version + commit) on GET /v1/status, so\nde status shows it. de start compares the running daemon''s build against this\nclient and, on skew (the client was upgraded but the daemon keeps running the\nold binary), replaces it with stop + start; --no-replace only warns. A daemon\ntoo old to report a version is treated as skew. de project up prints a\nbest-effort skew warning before registering routes.\n\nThis kills the recurring \"route clobber\": a stale daemon that predates a\nrouting change silently mis-registers routes (drops Path) with no other signal.\n\nFixes #56\n\n* feat(slo): add lint --fail-on-warn and auto-generate the OpenAPI when missing\n\nde slo lint --fail-on-warn (alias --strict) exits non-zero on ANY finding,\nincluding warnings, so a production CI gate can fail on un-calibrated or\nplaceholder-policy SLOs; default de slo lint still exits 0 on a fresh scaffold.\n\nde slo generate now runs de generate automatically when the enriched OpenAPI is\nmissing but the project can produce it (buf config present) — the fresh-scaffold\npath that previously errored with \"no openapi/*.openapi.yaml\". --no-generate\nopts out and fails loud with the actionable hint.\n\nFixes #61\nFixes #62\n\n* ci(docs): regenerate CLI reference pages and add a drift check\n\nAdd a docs-cli-check make target that regenerates the CLI reference pages and\nfails if they are stale versus the de command set, and run it in CI so the\nreference docs cannot silently fall behind new commands or flags. Regenerate all\nreference/cli pages wholesale (refreshes slo/start for the new flags).\n\nFixes #44\n\n* feat(skills): ship a discoverable new-service Claude Code skill for greenfield bootstrap\n\nAdd .claude/skills/new-service/SKILL.md: a consumer-facing skill that triggers on\n\"build a <X> service with devedge\" and drives the working flow — pin the SDK\nversion (never @latest), scaffold with de new service, model the resource,\ngenerate, build, run, and round-trip over HTTP. Add a \"Use with Claude Code\"\ngetting-started page (with a card link) and a root AGENTS.md pointer so the path\nis discoverable. In-repo skill + docs ship with no external credentials;\nmarketplace/plugin packaging is noted as a follow-up.\n\nFixes #14\n\n* docs(changelog): record the v0.15.0 issue sweep (#6 #14 #44 #56 #61 #62 #64)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSc2XCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlzQQAIrVwNBkso5cmjvItfH4OI8O\nZxxptrPrATwMbyO7lNCH+jx/ul0VCNjSEbpbSbt5xWeJzsI+9lB8l1Gf59TBBhfN\nxmuUEc0vDbOi+hau1PbH7eKEdC0FvyyhkaALOfkXCaPITN0kE0n9fJzFSSQLbOux\nW8Yc6XbJZIlpZGvZl9byOQ6Y71KkkeId1hYvnInqhXHSf/xmyUKU5Q9KlmFua6O0\nWB51iSD4obmAiQDVMKjBy49Kg+WZ+EFhZgaWbCnQXEfs4y6uzAOedCV/u8ihTO+E\n2DGSuh1vyBiY05Ecpr3TSOb/gOH1Ca38p0g+viXnIJQv+pD0cQpsf4PeD85DdP2v\nNr0RAF7W/4MjMyOyJL4xjzNEAJXjsZHDu7LAytFdfix3lX8/0fY12H+df/f/DLpU\no7ZhbLIRAe5jn7JfUD7Cg6G0uAaxzMhb28YDbLHc6aduxaSBwOrXBt/2X+fIEU1I\nepgMO/GmjDiX83IW0zCXvckF0EdxhsDplgo64QXb5Iz0vwjbzN+heoYl16/cuXgA\nrm1Bm18zldwJmUR1zybVvz6Hrnwpel/jb3ySy3BzJab7oJk+VGH832CizfeqZ68m\n+Ua0pJ+Rj03E8v2VATWKSqDpNPExT4rRYbnLCg6VZqRPoh5ZnKEQXgzWQYaxTYKd\nHC3ojV72YdhbAZJOsa8w\n=lYWq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-05T03:20:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/infobloxopen/devedge/commit/e81a4180c90502d4d02a7e74d250d66f88425f56","node_id":"C_kwDORkaP6toAKGU4MWE0MTgwYzkwNTAyZDRkMDJhN2U3NGQyNTBkNjZmODg0MjVmNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/infobloxopen/devedge/commit/41801ff6908fcc0046ae56ed73c5a2b4ae1f9ea9","sha":"41801ff6908fcc0046ae56ed73c5a2b4ae1f9ea9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/41801ff6908fcc0046ae56ed73c5a2b4ae1f9ea9"}],"sha":"e81a4180c90502d4d02a7e74d250d66f88425f56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/e81a4180c90502d4d02a7e74d250d66f88425f56"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/366029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/daniel-garcia","id":366029,"login":"daniel-garcia","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NjAyOQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/41801ff6908fcc0046ae56ed73c5a2b4ae1f9ea9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-05T01:19:46Z","email":"dgarcia@infoblox.com","name":"Daniel García"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-05T01:19:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"de compose: distinct member name for scaffolds; warn on inert postgres engine (#63)\n\nDX run 27 (composable services dogfood):\n\n- ''de compose add <repo>/module'' defaulted the member name to the import path''s last\n  segment — always ''module'' for a devedge-sdk scaffold — so the second add failed with\n  ''module name \"module\" is already a member'' on the most common composition case. Fall\n  back to the module-root segment (repo name) when the leaf is ''module'' (finding 118).\n\n- ''de compose build'' accepts a declared database.engine=postgres but the generated host\n  hardcodes the SQLite dialector and adds no postgres driver, so the declaration is inert\n  and crashes cryptically against a real DSN — while building/running clean on SQLite,\n  giving false confidence that multi-schema isolation works. Warn loudly at build on that\n  declared-vs-generated mismatch (finding 119; full postgres-composition generation tracked\n  separately).","tree":{"sha":"87ce854079fd957a4b1abd5052e982f5ec4bb28e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/trees/87ce854079fd957a4b1abd5052e982f5ec4bb28e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/commits/41801ff6908fcc0046ae56ed73c5a2b4ae1f9ea9","verification":{"payload":"tree 87ce854079fd957a4b1abd5052e982f5ec4bb28e\nparent c6c7adc238678abab9968be0b7b749e5ac63868f\nauthor Daniel García <dgarcia@infoblox.com> 1783214386 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783214386 -0500\n\nde compose: distinct member name for scaffolds; warn on inert postgres engine (#63)\n\nDX run 27 (composable services dogfood):\n\n- ''de compose add <repo>/module'' defaulted the member name to the import path''s last\n  segment — always ''module'' for a devedge-sdk scaffold — so the second add failed with\n  ''module name \"module\" is already a member'' on the most common composition case. Fall\n  back to the module-root segment (repo name) when the leaf is ''module'' (finding 118).\n\n- ''de compose build'' accepts a declared database.engine=postgres but the generated host\n  hardcodes the SQLite dialector and adds no postgres driver, so the declaration is inert\n  and crashes cryptically against a real DSN — while building/running clean on SQLite,\n  giving false confidence that multi-schema isolation works. Warn loudly at build on that\n  declared-vs-generated mismatch (finding 119; full postgres-composition generation tracked\n  separately).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSbEyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABEMQAAzMDMsND3wzwzMEFsgNQ+zA\n6C8ZkYgEZcPrbbdz8it4F1BYOE/7QoNDt/kbjbdIAerQeO4NNG37Hr+yB1kqucU/\nMnl6gOJDsk13z9JLQUD0uoy7n3ewcmOdym+qNrsIGGfQm22DYq75gfT5ozkctCpK\nuBn+y9y54wlBIbVSJLpybqwSyrndvlDxIp1DGjKNzQtP3m89OfiPS/Ls7bPvslF+\nDjeOrTHa/S3V6sZ5jp7OhKcWDmlrwVc4c7NHWBZ9iQ0AoNGtsqZi280FJEmzpLQw\nqNWAWRHMv6Hc+eR0VTYQ2hd2U5NDqmd2qSpX723R9yCm9kRCttVAqm9WB8xafBzQ\nsguGyHBSwL6VuJhwW6Dbqu9nfFArVSu04jkFc7I3HEzV24opVIEaCoYC5vS/Mjxl\np8B2FJqnDcYOkaSbWH7HB/2hlEA84NpHS045tj5u9FNKlxhcUUJSq3W5/4y268K6\ntl/HZjWjHJW6/RdqNSZkflS8TEKyNL3/b+YaoFm4jrTiSQuablKjxQvmq7+eQ7Lz\nhoxXHPx+FDVIgy6/qbMHKJh5vb7gs8+KEqtitx8cW3NFV7xwENcM4l2Dn5YVi6sz\nMALvoWGrIGeEIZN5YQZ/8mqJx0IeraHtBQ3YGNeR/bFxT84AhlPjDo69ZnW81b8M\nbIh5ngc/QvL/IeFmn7Ul\n=qcDX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-05T01:19:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.c