thub.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/1e9d8fcb24dd3600de4e1cc225c369fdca3b8811"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/366029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/daniel-garcia","id":366029,"login":"daniel-garcia","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NjAyOQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/58de5e6cf7eff6d9dfd8d729cf33fffeb6571d25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T20:31:57Z","email":"dgarcia@infoblox.com","name":"Daniel García"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T20:31:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ufe): scaffold serve target + dev-port + dev auth; show paths in de ls (#57)\n\nRun-19 DX hardening for the micro-frontend / full-stack path:\n\n- angular.json serve target uses browserTarget (required by the pinned\n  @angular-builders/custom-webpack@15 dev-server schema), not buildTarget, so\n  `pnpm start` succeeds on an untouched scaffold (086).\n- thread --dev-port into the scaffold''s angular.json via a single DefaultDevPort\n  shared with the shell-roster upstream, so the dev server binds the routed port\n  and the roster is not dead on arrival (088).\n- doctor probe and README use http (the dev server serves plain http), not\n  https, so \"no TLS listener\" no longer misreports as an untrusted cert (087).\n- promote the working `pnpm add <pkg>@link:<path>` recipe over the failing\n  `pnpm link --global` in the generated README (090).\n- wire a dev-only devAuthInterceptor (account-id/groups from\n  environment.devAuthHeaders) into the scaffold and document it in\n  consuming-a-service, so a generated client round-trips against the dev\n  authorizer (075).\n- de ls shows a PATH column so several routes on one host (a shell''s \"/\"\n  catch-all and its \"/api\" backend) are distinguishable (089).","tree":{"sha":"cbb706a9c4c49abaa0c2dc2dd9435575e6d6980c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/trees/cbb706a9c4c49abaa0c2dc2dd9435575e6d6980c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/commits/58de5e6cf7eff6d9dfd8d729cf33fffeb6571d25","verification":{"payload":"tree cbb706a9c4c49abaa0c2dc2dd9435575e6d6980c\nparent 12943dc4af0f6e5d07c2b802a057017e34593ab9\nauthor Daniel García <dgarcia@infoblox.com> 1783110717 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783110717 -0500\n\nfix(ufe): scaffold serve target + dev-port + dev auth; show paths in de ls (#57)\n\nRun-19 DX hardening for the micro-frontend / full-stack path:\n\n- angular.json serve target uses browserTarget (required by the pinned\n  @angular-builders/custom-webpack@15 dev-server schema), not buildTarget, so\n  `pnpm start` succeeds on an untouched scaffold (086).\n- thread --dev-port into the scaffold''s angular.json via a single DefaultDevPort\n  shared with the shell-roster upstream, so the dev server binds the routed port\n  and the roster is not dead on arrival (088).\n- doctor probe and README use http (the dev server serves plain http), not\n  https, so \"no TLS listener\" no longer misreports as an untrusted cert (087).\n- promote the working `pnpm add <pkg>@link:<path>` recipe over the failing\n  `pnpm link --global` in the generated README (090).\n- wire a dev-only devAuthInterceptor (account-id/groups from\n  environment.devAuthHeaders) into the scaffold and document it in\n  consuming-a-service, so a generated client round-trips against the dev\n  authorizer (075).\n- de ls shows a PATH column so several routes on one host (a shell''s \"/\"\n  catch-all and its \"/api\" backend) are distinguishable (089).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSBw9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApVcQACBKaFKxcbzJFZDxY5bgRgMO\nXwYLKPGMHtg3G4rJrCas4W6FJDE8hkIwJTP9nBXqYI/14noDCaedbQVxUBK5wJC+\n7R3GFejopIecHqO0DLI0T01aQN5v5xAVc44Fg+ivfYT74gUEYTe2Dy08hXr3kRL6\nzE5R/HsW8GORi1PaWTwICjcn+2AVHjNGRgkAQeUmS1Igh1gMuif8O8jSyIP1I6wb\ndZ5pmBxWRYUjrYrM+FsMOFgz3nbvYxugE7E+wERH9zV6kgYhRx1RTvVazxBlSOlx\n1E0LtGs+1vm8Gny6AZoZbcHHlHoYPI4KYZoWsguRmhQd0uM6lq5au5o2zSbuvM5p\ndH/MeRu+nKVnLFyqKgBE+VvXZveneX2MW1vF3usqxP8Z4frbIOUgWjzjB7zkcnRD\n6m51yhJ1ULTFKp1J6sGkef6byi2cKobT3eSyCDMkj/hwLJDmCh0BYjC/NnhJMl1P\n4Pm1H1ZzWXpkN11Jsh+nq+c+xnMH8eOdEBrgJ6RbCs3qpI/h8HHo8GosqHH6OaOD\nIRzYnYhOBHYYd70FXkj3QR5/6HY14nBiz3x1dChNxjvtg2ygTSUutmtWQ/shGBmU\nPhjDoBgEwSw+n0nmtJqEYLYMQcPxYeERRXK3keP37h0G8qzx3tIOg95WxQD3D79u\nrZzldQipIJJf/Sp/EBK3\n=j52Y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-03T20:31:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/infobloxopen/devedge/commit/58de5e6cf7eff6d9dfd8d729cf33fffeb6571d25","node_id":"C_kwDORkaP6toAKDU4ZGU1ZTZjZjdlZmY2ZDlkZmQ4ZDcyOWNmMzNmZmZlYjY1NzFkMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/infobloxopen/devedge/commit/12943dc4af0f6e5d07c2b802a057017e34593ab9","sha":"12943dc4af0f6e5d07c2b802a057017e34593ab9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/12943dc4af0f6e5d07c2b802a057017e34593ab9"}],"sha":"58de5e6cf7eff6d9dfd8d729cf33fffeb6571d25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/58de5e6cf7eff6d9dfd8d729cf33fffeb6571d25"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/366029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/daniel-garcia","id":366029,"login":"daniel-garcia","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NjAyOQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/12943dc4af0f6e5d07c2b802a057017e34593ab9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T20:06:50Z","email":"dgarcia@infoblox.com","name":"Daniel García"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T20:06:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"de compose: generate a working suite host + local-path/derived-SDK builds (#51)\n\nRun 18 findings 079/080/081/082/083 (WS-012 composable services).\n\n079 (P0): de compose build emitted a main.go calling each member''s Module() with\nzero args, but a scaffolded gorm module exposes Module(repo, sqlDB). Rewrite\nrenderMainGo to emit a real host: open ONE shared DB, build each member via the\nmodule''s uniform NewModule(db) seam, run a host-owned union AutoMigrate, wire the\ndev authorizer/principal, and serve via servicekit.Run. gofmt the output. The\ngenerated (un-hand-edited) binary now compiles, boots, and round-trips every\nmember. Fixtures gain the same NewModule/Models seam; the build-acceptance test\nproves the generated host compiles.\n\n080 (P1): derive the composed go.mod + composition.lock devedge-sdk pin from the\nmembers'' own go.mod (highest semver) instead of a hardcoded v0.28.0; fall back to\nDefaultSDKVersion only when no member is local. tidy no longer prints a bare ''OK''\nwhen external members went unchecked — it states plainly what was NOT verified.\n\n081 (P2): de compose test now EXITS NON-ZERO when external members could not be\nverified in-process, directing to build+boot the generated host — it can no\nlonger green-wash a composition whose real binary does not build.\n\n082 (P2): de compose add --path <dir> records a local member; de compose build\nwrites a go.mod replace to it so a two-repo composition builds before either\nmember is published.\n\n083 (P3): stop writing the invalid token ''latest'' into go.mod — a local member is\nrequired at the local pseudo-version behind a replace; an unpinned published\nmember fails loud with guidance.","tree":{"sha":"ccedd51ee24f0be6fbe7ba47857bb143e84662cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/trees/ccedd51ee24f0be6fbe7ba47857bb143e84662cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/commits/12943dc4af0f6e5d07c2b802a057017e34593ab9","verification":{"payload":"tree ccedd51ee24f0be6fbe7ba47857bb143e84662cd\nparent 6e012706a5d963012273a1d5ddd286b085490e49\nauthor Daniel García <dgarcia@infoblox.com> 1783109210 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783109210 -0500\n\nde compose: generate a working suite host + local-path/derived-SDK builds (#51)\n\nRun 18 findings 079/080/081/082/083 (WS-012 composable services).\n\n079 (P0): de compose build emitted a main.go calling each member''s Module() with\nzero args, but a scaffolded gorm module exposes Module(repo, sqlDB). Rewrite\nrenderMainGo to emit a real host: open ONE shared DB, build each member via the\nmodule''s uniform NewModule(db) seam, run a host-owned union AutoMigrate, wire the\ndev authorizer/principal, and serve via servicekit.Run. gofmt the output. The\ngenerated (un-hand-edited) binary now compiles, boots, and round-trips every\nmember. Fixtures gain the same NewModule/Models seam; the build-acceptance test\nproves the generated host compiles.\n\n080 (P1): derive the composed go.mod + composition.lock devedge-sdk pin from the\nmembers'' own go.mod (highest semver) instead of a hardcoded v0.28.0; fall back to\nDefaultSDKVersion only when no member is local. tidy no longer prints a bare ''OK''\nwhen external members went unchecked — it states plainly what was NOT verified.\n\n081 (P2): de compose test now EXITS NON-ZERO when external members could not be\nverified in-process, directing to build+boot the generated host — it can no\nlonger green-wash a composition whose real binary does not build.\n\n082 (P2): de compose add --path <dir> records a local member; de compose build\nwrites a go.mod replace to it so a two-repo composition builds before either\nmember is published.\n\n083 (P3): stop writing the invalid token ''latest'' into go.mod — a local member is\nrequired at the local pseudo-version behind a replace; an unpinned published\nmember fails loud with guidance.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSBZaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxTEQAF4H+rK87ELkmQEYwnS1vw4L\novgZwy9yMBVioZv3Z94hxVApwW/kGM9O5cuMjLbIvjTgiaqXrK3QmN+Lv+GfFUm0\ntwJb+Utf7OXM81OV3wn4NLnJYskLwinXEli/UKAGHtwl9ImsDBMAoKRHiSUpxsc1\n2iwqEEqt6wC4qtKro0tWngqO793ryIVMsoHlKwUn2XZ8sPS+kymq1l4aLyN4BiYI\nXWgUiQJtR3F8RMEt6ytAAnAzAk2qyqkgLgimlLmiMSUrens7LcXMHAh0O/ZwkRJH\nxd3o1iLqQ+pWKVUz1P8zzqu9Rm5Z4uUIeJs4XdtWw+fkmxVQm2ozkCr0Ot4hZ/1/\nWaD/MpZjjZVdt5fZrc0BsBWqXNrrhcmn65vlebocof4xk4+6LEXwbPOnd1CWDE1Z\nedWOYVEonNl3IYOjgKkTIPxrqqaONsr/L5JgUJx4wQjU5Z8TUjPT7OF7rh7nJNdc\nQHhgujX6USW7VVzFo+S8ARe2XBOYzpGFjZIRvjMfvRw2r3vUrbzbXsYsqOBNxhsk\nllDq+KkyChiIT3Y15rhDm+R2kNPKepaKjWpusTRvYtnNVjMUssoNzBhElisWhG2i\n4K7hXpuZQhhjrV4t77GYy4XiyajLoHEP3nWryNTtwNoC5QyAuli6JnmU0DkDjUMq\n8k0TRVAq3FaIG/4uX91h\n=EtuC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-03T20:06:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://