s","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/50708d3d3a8ceba00fa04f8fb803262754d46200/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T02:19:17Z","email":"dgarcia@infoblox.com","name":"Daniel García"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T02:19:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(cli): extract an overridable session.go seam for CLI auth (WS-024 P3a) (#32)\n\n* cliscaffold: extract session factory into an overridable session.go seam\n\nMove the OIDC SessionFactory out of the inlined main.go into a separate\nscaffolded session.go (newSessionFactory), so a preset applied with\n`de cli new --preset-dir` can override the auth binding wholesale without\ntouching main.go or forking the open-core clikit runtime. This is the CLI\nanalog of a devedge micro-frontend shell overlaying bootstrap-session.\n\n- add templates/session.go.tmpl: newSessionFactory() returning the generic\n  OIDC device-grant factory (unchanged behavior; provider-agnostic).\n- main.go.tmpl: call newSessionFactory(); drop the inline factory and the\n  now-unused path/filepath, clikit/auth, clikit/auth/oidc imports.\n- test: expect session.go in the tree and assert the seam lives there.\n\n* cli: fix --preset-dir example to the real infoblox-cli preset path","tree":{"sha":"bf4500ab46b40e9c00730f6df091d3fd54a53216","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/trees/bf4500ab46b40e9c00730f6df091d3fd54a53216"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/commits/50708d3d3a8ceba00fa04f8fb803262754d46200","verification":{"payload":"tree bf4500ab46b40e9c00730f6df091d3fd54a53216\nparent 074aa2a76676c671092611355b04afa9afc9fe00\nauthor Daniel García <dgarcia@infoblox.com> 1783045157 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783045157 -0500\n\nfeat(cli): extract an overridable session.go seam for CLI auth (WS-024 P3a) (#32)\n\n* cliscaffold: extract session factory into an overridable session.go seam\n\nMove the OIDC SessionFactory out of the inlined main.go into a separate\nscaffolded session.go (newSessionFactory), so a preset applied with\n`de cli new --preset-dir` can override the auth binding wholesale without\ntouching main.go or forking the open-core clikit runtime. This is the CLI\nanalog of a devedge micro-frontend shell overlaying bootstrap-session.\n\n- add templates/session.go.tmpl: newSessionFactory() returning the generic\n  OIDC device-grant factory (unchanged behavior; provider-agnostic).\n- main.go.tmpl: call newSessionFactory(); drop the inline factory and the\n  now-unused path/filepath, clikit/auth, clikit/auth/oidc imports.\n- test: expect session.go in the tree and assert the seam lives there.\n\n* cli: fix --preset-dir example to the real infoblox-cli preset path","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRxwlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmJwQADNid0Si80NPIrxl19oGMMgv\ncDUWS+m1Mo0py4ovlqR1ruCjC9nc1rKaBrMVtkSVopN0C29ETSiUBjIavVPucmUd\nBb5YY1zho6FrGv5wsIcunp8gB0xcDhDNAfx1ItRenQQxHheoHCKjW1aqawoD+t4f\ncI/ZgPEZqkoJNf5KABSNkS/Dv8BgcYIg+epl6Yf8yCyMM9GtxJYW/Auph8yaJOe8\ncfvsKhuOUu19xOHkQgRRloSJ6aX0pKXZVgt3bFoU/KLzAmYPvDoFqxxHfpmkhjpm\nkJhThS6cz3GE7ybml9Uit6QS0nlhh5wx9IfBtYfgQzp4kYmMpz/4i5jQwtDlM83g\ndjHOHK92Gv6jKL98aCG767mAvkxBM0LFAlCtUrG7l1j+lGD5yxjES/n/YFHzr6Jn\n0ANDk521ODcMfgscA/i8wF9dIJjUaoB6iweW5yLN36y6PmszXBKe/xHiUPtEMXfw\nsbz0Z8kMSSkaqhmStzNIvqw+2s3JvVySMeq8X0ajGNPXlqc1vtaN/MqU+XqJwob1\naj9nq1K3q6mavGw7jRPcPaCNhaGqiP9VrsQhdn0xKi6RQ+rCe6AHsNaosU3kjlfi\ndcntQkEFQ3LJlB1oqKjFFmD2lyiIfx5wEFgT3U5TqvusZez1kyb/p/Jp5+PPQx8E\nwJV5bdFZKQNajIQBA7u4\n=zp5J\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-03T02:19:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/infobloxopen/devedge/commit/50708d3d3a8ceba00fa04f8fb803262754d46200","node_id":"C_kwDORkaP6toAKDUwNzA4ZDNkM2E4Y2ViYTAwZmEwNGY4ZmI4MDMyNjI3NTRkNDYyMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/infobloxopen/devedge/commit/074aa2a76676c671092611355b04afa9afc9fe00","sha":"074aa2a76676c671092611355b04afa9afc9fe00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/074aa2a76676c671092611355b04afa9afc9fe00"}],"sha":"50708d3d3a8ceba00fa04f8fb803262754d46200","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/50708d3d3a8ceba00fa04f8fb803262754d46200"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/366029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/daniel-garcia","id":366029,"login":"daniel-garcia","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NjAyOQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/074aa2a76676c671092611355b04afa9afc9fe00/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T02:02:21Z","email":"dgarcia@infoblox.com","name":"Daniel García"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T02:02:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"de terraform: scaffold + extend registry-publishable Terraform providers (#31)\n\nAdd `de terraform new` and `de terraform add`, the Terraform mirror of\n`de cli` (WS-024 P2), driving the devedge-terraform-sdk (v0.1.0) tfkit\nruntime and tfgen generator.\n\n`de terraform new NAME` renders a registry-publishable\nterraform-provider-<name> Go repo via a new internal/tfscaffold engine\n(embed.FS + text/template, missingkey=error, --preset-dir overlay seam),\nmirroring internal/cliscaffold. The emitted repo carries the HashiCorp\nprovider release shape: a hand-written tfkit provider.go seam, a\nGoReleaser config (zip archives + GPG-signed SHA256SUMS + registry\nmanifest), terraform-registry-manifest.json, a tag-triggered signed\nrelease workflow, and CI. Dependency versions (terraform-plugin-framework,\n-validators, devedge-terraform-sdk) are pinned to the SDK''s own go.mod.\n\n`de terraform add --input SPEC --resource NAME` runs the pinned tfgen\n(`go run .../cmd/tfgen@<ver>`, version read from the provider go.mod,\nfallback to the scaffold default) to emit the resource module and rewrite\ninternal/provider/resources_gen.go; it never touches the provider.go seam\nand is idempotent.\n\nThe generated go directive is go 1.25 to match the SDK''s own go.mod\n(the tightest constraint on the provider), verified to build end-to-end.","tree":{"sha":"7aaec52b507a834eeba524a091f1fe3419eae852","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/trees/7aaec52b507a834eeba524a091f1fe3419eae852"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/commits/074aa2a76676c671092611355b04afa9afc9fe00","verification":{"payload":"tree 7aaec52b507a834eeba524a091f1fe3419eae852\nparent 84ff2baa9b0ce1a53bea30015e5678abd07a88a4\nauthor Daniel García <dgarcia@infoblox.com> 1783044141 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783044141 -0500\n\nde terraform: scaffold + extend registry-publishable Terraform providers (#31)\n\nAdd `de terraform new` and `de terraform add`, the Terraform mirror of\n`de cli` (WS-024 P2), driving the devedge-terraform-sdk (v0.1.0) tfkit\nruntime and tfgen generator.\n\n`de terraform new NAME` renders a registry-publishable\nterraform-provider-<name> Go repo via a new internal/tfscaffold engine\n(embed.FS + text/template, missingkey=error, --preset-dir overlay seam),\nmirroring internal/cliscaffold. The emitted repo carries the HashiCorp\nprovider release shape: a hand-written tfkit provider.go seam, a\nGoReleaser config (zip archives + GPG-signed SHA256SUMS + registry\nmanifest), terraform-registry-manifest.json, a tag-triggered signed\nrelease workflow, and CI. Dependency versions (terraform-plugin-framework,\n-validators, devedge-terraform-sdk) are pinned to the SDK''s own go.mod.\n\n`de terraform add --input SPEC --resource NAME` runs the pinned tfgen\n(`go run .../cmd/tfgen@<ver>`, version read from the provider go.mod,\nfallback to the scaffold default) to emit the resource module and rewrite\ninternal/provider/resources_gen.go; it never touches the provider.go seam\nand is idempotent.\n\nThe generated go directive is go 1.25 to match the SDK''s own go.mod\n(the tightest constraint on the provider), verified to build end-to-end.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRxgtCRC1aQ7uu