278559472c","sha":"b5ae44935d99c3a4620b651bced9ab278559472c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/b5ae44935d99c3a4620b651bced9ab278559472c"}],"sha":"66a7ffa3d73a22a296dbc265939f8abc2e9ecc3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/66a7ffa3d73a22a296dbc265939f8abc2e9ecc3e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/366029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/daniel-garcia","id":366029,"login":"daniel-garcia","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NjAyOQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/b5ae44935d99c3a4620b651bced9ab278559472c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T19:12:11Z","email":"dgarcia@infoblox.com","name":"Daniel García"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T19:12:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"WS-022 + WS-023: de migrate CLI + hermetic build authority (#28)\n\n* feat(de): make de the hermetic build authority; Makefile as regenerable shim (WS-023)\n\nPromote real build verbs into de, operating on a service project dir:\n  de generate  buf generate with PINNED buf + codegen plugins, then go mod tidy\n  de build     go build -trimpath ./... (reproducible)\n  de test      go test ./...\n  de lint      pinned golangci-lint if configured, else go vet ./...\n  de image     distroless-static OCI image via pinned ko (-trimpath, multi-arch)\n\nThe build logic lives in de, not a Makefile. Hermeticity comes from pinning the\ntoolchain in internal/toolchain (version constants, matching the repo''s existing\nSDKVersion/composition.lock idiom) and running each tool via go run/go install\nof module@version — no more @latest, independent of host PATH. Same de version\n-> same toolchain -> same output. Constants (not go.mod tool directives) keep\ndevedge''s dependency graph light and work when de runs from a foreign module.\n\nde sync writes .devedge/make/devedge.mk: a DO-NOT-EDIT managed fragment whose\ntargets are one-liners delegating to the de verbs (generate/build/test/lint/\nimage/migrate-lint). Idempotent; the top-level Makefile stays hand-owned and\njust -includes the fragment. de doctor flags a stale/hand-edited fragment.\n\nde api publish now calls the in-Go de generate logic instead of shelling to\nmake generate. Uniform -trimpath applied to de build, de image, devedge''s own\n.goreleaser.yaml, and the root Makefile release build. devedge''s own Makefile is\nNOT converted to delegate to de (it builds de itself — bootstrap/CI chicken-and-\negg); the shim model targets consumer services.\n\nDeferred (separate, orchestrator-sequenced): the devedge-sdk / internal scaffold\nadoption (emitting the thin Makefile + dropping @latest in the scaffold template).\n\n* feat(migrate): add `de migrate` command family, linter, and hook hardening (WS-022 P2/P3)\n\nAdd the `de migrate` cobra tree driving the infobloxopen/migrate fork through\ninternal/migrate:\n\n  - new <name>   scaffold the next-numbered up/down pair (4-digit, header docs the\n                 rules; no per-file SET timeout line)\n  - lint         authoritative pure-Go sequence/pairing gate (naming, gaps,\n                 duplicates, missing pairs, CONCURRENTLY mixed with other statements)\n                 + best-effort squawk over *.up.sql (skipped, never failed, when absent)\n  - up           apply to the on-disk target; lock_timeout/statement_timeout set on\n                 the migration CONNECTION (never per file)\n  - status       current applied version vs target + dirty state\n  - verify       assert at target and not dirty (the unattended Job''s final gate)\n\nEncode the correctness rules: timeouts on the connection via the `options` startup\nparameter (new migrate.WithConnTimeouts), and lint fails a CONCURRENTLY statement\nthat shares a file with others. Add migrate.ForkApplier.Status for read-only\nversion/dirty reporting.\n\nStandardize migration numbering to 4-digit: rename the scaffold starter migration\nto 0001_webhook_endpoints.*, and update the AGENTS.md/README references and the\ngenerated service''s NNN wording.\n\nHarden the Helm pre-install/pre-upgrade migration Job: backoffLimit 3,\nactiveDeadlineSeconds, ttlSecondsAfterFinished, retained hook-delete-policy +\nhook-weight, and connection-timeout env the generated service now reads\n(DEVEDGE_LOCK_TIMEOUT/STATEMENT_TIMEOUT), with the unattended guarantees documented\ninline. Wire the same seatbelt into the scaffold''s generated migrate connection.\n\n* fix(migrate): compose SDK framework baseline in devedge appliers (WS-022 seam)\n\nde migrate up/status/verify and de project up reconcile now compose the SDK\nframework baseline (0001) ahead of a service''s on-disk module migrations (0002+)\nwhen the service depends on github.com/infobloxopen/devedge-sdk/persistence/migrate,\nso they converge on the SAME single version space the service applies at Serve\n(1=framework, 2+=domain) instead of a second, conflicting version space. A raw /\nnon-SDK dep composes nothing (pre-WS-022 behavior preserved).\n\n- internal/migrate/baseline.go: resolveBaselineDir (go list -m), ComposeSource,\n  materializeComposed (mirrors SDK materialize: numeric order, fail-loud on a\n  duplicate version), FrameworkBaselinePresent.\n- de migrate lint/new: first on-disk migration must be 0002 for an SDK service\n  (0001 reserved), 0001 for a raw service; scaffold 0002 first in an empty SDK dir.\n- de migrate status/verify: underflow-safe when current > target (rollback pending).\n- toolchain: assert codegen plugin versions match scaffold runtime versions.\n- tests for composition, reserved-0001 lint, nextVersion, and uint-underflow safety.\n\n* feat(de): de generate reaches full SDK-scaffold codegen parity; thin Makefile shim (WS-023)\n\nTeach `de generate` to reproduce the SDK scaffold''s `make generate` flow\nhermetically and backend-aware, so a freshly scaffolded service builds entirely\nvia `de` verbs with a thin `-include` Makefile.\n\nde generate (cmd/de/build.go):\n- parse the service''s buf.gen.yaml to learn which codegen plugins it drives;\n- install PUBLIC plugins pinned by `de` (adds protoc-gen-openapiv2) AND the\n  devedge-sdk plugins (protoc-gen-{devedge-authz,svc,ent|storage}) pinned to the\n  service''s resolved SDK version (go list -m) — that pin is the hermetic pin —\n  into the version-keyed cache bindir + PATH;\n- guarded `buf dep update` (self-heals a --no-generate tree), then pinned buf\n  generate;\n- convert the OpenAPI v2 surface to v3 with the SDK''s openapiv2to3 when an\n  OpenAPI surface is emitted;\n- run the ent entc two-step (go get seed + go generate ./gen/ent) when the\n  backend is ent; then go mod tidy.\n- fail loud on an unknown local plugin `de` cannot install hermetically.\n\ntoolchain: add protoc-gen-openapiv2 (grpc-gateway/v2 line), SDK plugin/cmd\nclassification (IsSDKPlugin, PublicPlugin, SDKCmd, SDKModule, OpenAPIV2To3Bin).\n\nde image: autodetect DOCKER_HOST from the active docker context for local\n(ko.local) builds, preserving the scaffold''s socket-autodetecting `make image`\nnow that `image` delegates to `de image`.\n\ndevedge-native scaffold (internal/scaffold): convert Makefile.tmpl to a thin\n`-include .devedge/make/devedge.mk` shim + emit the managed fragment from the\ncanonical makefrag source (byte-identical to `de sync`); drop @latest tool\nblocks; point AGENTS/README + `de new`/`de project init` guidance at `de generate`.","tree":{"sha":"8909334a5077b1f0b780ff4dd806997b58f84714","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/trees/8909334a5077b1f0b780ff4dd806997b58f84714"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/commits/b5ae44935d99c3a4620b651bced9ab278559472c","verification":{"payload":"tree 8909334a5077b1f0b780ff4dd806997b58f84714\nparent 884a2d48b29f9c54eb770b06acc07f0c17025318\nauthor Daniel García <dgarcia@infoblox.com> 1783019531 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783019531 -0500\n\nWS-022 + WS-023: de migrate CLI + hermetic build authority (#28)\n\n* feat(de): make de the hermetic build authority; Makefile as regenerable shim (WS-023)\n\nPromote real build verbs into de, operating on a service project dir:\n  de generate  buf generate with PINNED buf + codegen plugins, then go mod tidy\n  de build     go build -trimpath ./... (reproducible)\n  de test      go test ./...\n  de lint      pinned golangci-lint if configured, else go vet ./...\n  de image     distroless-static OCI image via pinned ko (-trimpath, multi-arch)\n\nThe build logic lives in de, not a Makefile. Hermeticity comes from pinning the\ntoolchain in internal/toolchain (version constants, matching the repo''s existing\nSDKVersion/composition.lock idiom) and running each tool via go run/go install\nof module@version — no more @latest, independent of host PATH. Same de version\n-> same toolchain -> same output. Constants (not go.mod tool directives) keep\ndevedge''s dependency graph light and work when de runs from a foreign module.\n\nde sync writes .devedge/make/devedge.mk: a DO-NOT-EDIT managed fragment whose\ntargets are one-liners delegating to the de verbs (generate/build/test/lint/\nimage/migrate-lint). Idempotent; the top-level Makefile stays hand-owned and\njust -includes the fragment. de doctor flags a stale/hand-edited fragment.\n\nde api publish now calls the in-Go de generate logic instead of shelling to\nmake generate. Uniform -trimpath applied to de build, de image, devedge''s own\n.goreleaser.yaml, and the root Makefile release build. devedge''s own Makefile is\nNOT converted to delegate to de (it builds de itself — bootstrap/CI chicken-and-\negg); the shim model targets consumer services.\n\nDeferred (separate, orchestrator-sequenced): the devedge-sdk / internal scaffold\nadoption (emitting the thin Makefile + dropping @latest in the scaffold template).\n\n* feat(migrate): add `de migrate` command family, linter, and hook hardening (WS-022 P2/P3)\n\nAdd the `de migrate` cobra tree driving the infobloxopen/migrate fork through\ninternal/migrate:\n\n  - new <name>   scaffold the next-numbered up/down pair (4-digit, header docs the\n                 rules; no per-file SET timeout line)\n  - lint         authoritative pure-Go sequence/pairing gate (naming, gaps,\n                 duplicates, missing pairs, CONCURRENTLY mixed with other statements)\n                 + best-effort squawk over *.up.sql (skipped, never failed, when absent)\n  - up           apply to the on-disk target; lock_timeout/statement_timeout set on\n                 the migration CONNECTION (never per file)\n  - status       current applied version vs target + dirty state\n  - verify       assert at target and not dirty (the unattended Job''s final gate)\n\nEncode the correctness rules: timeouts on the connection via the `options` startup\nparameter (new migrate.WithConnTimeouts), and lint fails a CONCURRENTLY statement\nthat shares a file with others. Add migrate.ForkApplier.Status for read-only\nversion/dirty reporting.\n\nStandardize migration numbering to 4-digit: rename the scaffold starter migration\nto 0001_webhook_endpoints.*, and update the AGENTS.md/README references and the\ngenerated service''s NNN wording.\n\nHarden the Helm pre-install/pre-upgrade migration Job: backoffLimit 3,\nactiveDeadlineSeconds, ttlSecondsAfterFinished, retained hook-delete-policy +\nhook-weight, and connection-timeout env the generated service now reads\n(DEVEDGE_LOCK_TIMEOUT/STATEMENT_TIMEOUT), with the unattended guarantees documented\ninline. Wire the same seatbelt into the scaffold''s generated migrate connection.\n\n* fix(migrate): compose SDK framework baseline in devedge appliers (WS-022 seam)\n\nde migrate up/status/verify and de project up reconcile now compose the SDK\nframework baseline (0001) ahead of a service''s on-disk module migrations (0002+)\nwhen the service depends on github.com/infobloxopen/devedge-sdk/persistence/migrate,\nso they converge on the SAME single version space the service applies at Serve\n(1=framework, 2+=domain) instead of a second, conflicting version space. A raw /\nnon-SDK dep composes nothing (pre-WS-022 behavior preserved).\n\n- internal/migrate/baseline.go: resolveBaselineDir (go list -m), ComposeSource,\n  materializeComposed (mirrors SDK materialize: numeric order, fail-loud on a\n  duplicate version), FrameworkBaselinePresent.\n- de migrate lint/new: first on-disk migration must be 0002 for an SDK service\n  (0001 reserved), 0001 for a raw service; scaffold 0002 first in an empty SDK dir.\n- de migrate status/verify: underflow-safe when current > target (rollback pending).\n- toolchain: assert codegen plugin versions match scaffold runtime versions.\n- tests for composition, reserved-0001 lint, nextVersion, and uint-underflow safety.\n\n* feat(de): de generate reaches full SDK-scaffold codegen parity; thin Makefile shim (WS-023)\n\nTeach `de generate` to reproduce the SDK scaffold''s `make generate` flow\nhermetically and backend-aware, so a freshly scaffolded service builds entirely\nvia `de` verbs with a thin `-include` Makefile.\n\nde generate (cmd/de/build.go):\n- parse the service''s buf.gen.yaml to learn which codegen plugins it drives;\n- install PUBLIC plugins pinned by `de` (adds protoc-gen-openapiv2) AND the\n  devedge-sdk plugins (protoc-gen-{devedge-authz,svc,ent|storage}) pinned to the\n  service''s resolved SDK version (go list -m) — that pin is the hermetic pin —\n  into the version-keyed cache bindir + PATH;\n- guarded `buf dep update` (self-heals a --no-generate tree), then pinned buf\n  generate;\n- convert the OpenAPI v2 surface to v3 with the SDK''s openapiv2to3 when an\n  OpenAPI surface is emitted;\n- run the ent entc two-step (go get seed + go generate ./gen/ent) when the\n  backend is ent; then go mod tidy.\n- fail loud on an unknown local plugin `de` cannot install hermetically.\n\ntoolchain: add protoc-gen-openapiv2 (grpc-gateway/v2 line), SDK plugin/cmd\nclassification (IsSDKPlugin, PublicPlugin, SDKCmd, SDKModule, OpenAPIV2To3Bin).\n\nde image: autodetect DOCKER_HOST from the active docker context for local\n(ko.local) builds, preserving the scaffold''s socket-autodetecting `make image`\nnow that `image` delegates to `de image`.\n\ndevedge-native scaffold (internal/scaffold): convert Makefile.tmpl to a thin\n`-include .devedge/make/devedge.mk` shim + emit the managed fragment from the\ncanonical makefrag source (byte-identical to `de sync`); drop @latest tool\nblocks; point AGENTS/README + `de new`/`de project init` guidance at `de generate`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRrgLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlNMQAAVH+DLNve6v6lAD+wFoBBVY\nBlNLt+HyuKFlg7VtH5GUV3zf0VPfPyBKi8udC4YDpauicYGZ+aOIj2+ukN8vg09z\nzGKlIuNE3fPw0vHD3F+caL9BLluDc2UoKYHBwPxwToNF765O1SuM0vwCVRtx8laz\nHC/8U0o5nRI102XH2oDHMpcOTsBl/SRlhapYqe/Enz+py9RcD782sqJE1MxN5Yq2\njYydp/XJObBGBZ+4HGq3jzG6mlm+FJLAoaAuIl6AUVwNUDNnDwvXt8CUKc1ORWpn\nNcPtVStFcn5ps6JqMLZIdlkkOJK6pwFdiTzgcGII1sZ1IffzIh95jq/fMox9X51P\n7ogCXIkmY+A9/t63Yu7gCezmtOa8JB0ugeqykYNtQErILFdxiSr/b5H363VkLTiu\nhm41FlkmitXwrNabxOcLlA2fmdFS1JD9LZjluMEKKfT6R8wvlLa5a3kHBv6ok7uZ\nMjzsXZTzwBfEYJODr/d3Uwh