e lint (WS-019 P4)\n\nDocument the API URL layout conventions on the portal and add a linter that\nrejects the version-after-resource anti-pattern in proto HTTP bindings.\n\n- docs/content/docs/explanation/api-url-layout.md: explain the apilayout seam —\n  the product-rest default (/api/{domain}/v{major}/{resource}), the k8s-apis\n  variant, the naming rules table, the version-before-resource rule and rejected\n  anti-pattern, and how the layout is set (de new service --api-layout/--domain,\n  kind: Shell api.layout, edge composes/strips /api/{domain}). Add its card to\n  the explanation index.\n- hack/lint-api-paths.sh: scan **/*.proto google.api.http path templates and fail\n  when a version segment follows a collection (version-after-resource). Wired as\n  make lint-api-paths with a built-in --self-test (good path passes, bad flagged).\n\n* docs: point the serve-the-shell link at its specific how-to page","tree":{"sha":"d394946436f00e6ef4bd3843f81c4a31c1d6c99c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/trees/d394946436f00e6ef4bd3843f81c4a31c1d6c99c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/commits/2d4994b9b139109428247242259e14af38b5452e","verification":{"payload":"tree d394946436f00e6ef4bd3843f81c4a31c1d6c99c\nparent a89a88f85fddcd56e3d6233bdeeb46502ccd320c\nauthor Daniel García <dgarcia@infoblox.com> 1782944237 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782944237 -0500\n\ndocs+lint: API URL layout conventions + version-after-resource lint (WS-019 P4) (#24)\n\n* docs+lint: API URL layout explanation + version-after-resource lint (WS-019 P4)\n\nDocument the API URL layout conventions on the portal and add a linter that\nrejects the version-after-resource anti-pattern in proto HTTP bindings.\n\n- docs/content/docs/explanation/api-url-layout.md: explain the apilayout seam —\n  the product-rest default (/api/{domain}/v{major}/{resource}), the k8s-apis\n  variant, the naming rules table, the version-before-resource rule and rejected\n  anti-pattern, and how the layout is set (de new service --api-layout/--domain,\n  kind: Shell api.layout, edge composes/strips /api/{domain}). Add its card to\n  the explanation index.\n- hack/lint-api-paths.sh: scan **/*.proto google.api.http path templates and fail\n  when a version segment follows a collection (version-after-resource). Wired as\n  make lint-api-paths with a built-in --self-test (good path passes, bad flagged).\n\n* docs: point the serve-the-shell link at its specific how-to page","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRZHtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvbgQAEbfnojZbC9XsjN3Odt47A0m\ntOIr+Xme3SEGhk43qozRxY7TikDw6X9yZZCXbjhkeeSyCAitjvC+8W4hXhrtl0qH\nTcSo59t2XxvCUJhuH3rQABQzAEvGFfH8jKM8GfRX110kIq7X621zkN0jqQKXZ2mU\nlJCq81wVm+Hnm90xExp9t4v3wcqZmMyrQub8g522xZNHiLQt/p+FMnK+KEfhaI99\nDMwPW4wok30tR7FBfAuF8TRVGT2GvO0jkJVuuT7f1v1HNajfYscdRWVRk2L2FQmn\nt68OWrFki6WmGdbYxpP14s0ZSCNQIi+Q8SCpoCZF+/FWSZv9L0jff0dI5kHBTN5Y\nViYUzheoab8sgQC9MsIi5R8dzkP9xq7GeO6FMeoeXbR224uKa4GRzYF7HwGkrQVQ\n9Vm0MOD5LKRS0GwVLsWlODFIfeVIcKxuQTp0ECcj2pPFfys8DpooJwlseowBaKH3\nOyeKbuSROCx7TC9LwIQr28cs8/smDgnhTi83VFbInZnJcD+wyhsKzkmLfBp0eX2i\nf81ACiBJ0GHTvtHyZx6G6fy8HLB2keLxBVNaPN5+udzDn43FwJrByucnktbWKPmK\nYY+1/L4cKt5KpFDSubBG1rPJx5NIjtc4mdwROLMc8rKpZRTVGLDfl/NGmIFxw759\nSlAFRj4HoHvqvf98izWR\n=du80\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-01T22:17:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/infobloxopen/devedge/commit/2d4994b9b139109428247242259e14af38b5452e","node_id":"C_kwDORkaP6toAKDJkNDk5NGI5YjEzOTEwOTQyODI0NzI0MjI1OWUxNGFmMzhiNTQ1MmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/infobloxopen/devedge/commit/a89a88f85fddcd56e3d6233bdeeb46502ccd320c","sha":"a89a88f85fddcd56e3d6233bdeeb46502ccd320c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/a89a88f85fddcd56e3d6233bdeeb46502ccd320c"}],"sha":"2d4994b9b139109428247242259e14af38b5452e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/2d4994b9b139109428247242259e14af38b5452e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/366029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/daniel-garcia","id":366029,"login":"daniel-garcia","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NjAyOQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/a89a88f85fddcd56e3d6233bdeeb46502ccd320c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T22:08:34Z","email":"dgarcia@infoblox.com","name":"Daniel García"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T22:08:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(routing): wire apilayout URL-layout seam into shell + scaffold, fix Go-host collision (WS-019 P2+P3) (#23)\n\nBump devedge-sdk to v0.44.0 (provides the apilayout package) and use its\nURL-layout strategy seam to compose product-rest public URLs at the edge,\nresolving the WS-018 Go-host catch-all collision.\n\nShell config (P2, pkg/config):\n- spec.api.layout (default product-rest, validated via apilayout.Parse).\n- Per-domain method-1 routing: spec.api.services[] now carries {domain,\n  upstream}; each backend is routed at apilayout.<layout>.Prefix()/{domain}\n  (e.g. /api/notes) with strip-prefix, so several domains coexist on one\n  shell origin and each composes /api/{domain}/v{version}/{resource} at the\n  edge without touching proto annotations. The legacy single prefix+upstream\n  (no domain) still parses and routes as a no-domain catch-all — backward\n  compatible with the shipped method-1 shell.\n- ToRoutes builds the prefix via apilayout (never hardcodes /api) and emits\n  one strip route per domain plus the optional legacy catch-all.\n\nScaffold + Go-host fix (P3, internal/scaffold, internal/sdkscaffold, cmd/de):\n- --api-layout (default product-rest) and --domain (default = service name)\n  on `de new service` and `de project init`.\n- Emitted devedge.yaml routes the service at the app host under\n  <layout-prefix>/{domain} with stripPrefix:true INSTEAD of a host catch-all,\n  so two services (/api/foo, /api/bar) coexist under one host — collision\n  resolved and the public URL is product-rest. --host still works.\n- README/AGENTS curl examples use https://{host}/api/{domain}/v1/...\n- `de ufe new` create-default shell now sets api.layout: product-rest.\n\nTests: layout parse/default/invalid; product-rest per-domain routes\n(/api/{domain} + strip); k8s-apis /apis/{group} prefix; method-1 backward\ncompat; two-scaffolded-services-don''t-collide (both scaffolds); domain/layout\noverrides. make test (unit+integration+e2e) and make lint green. CLI reference\nregenerated for the changed help (new.md, project.md).","tree":{"sha":"e408c359c3209681cab0ef1d4afa9588b34d4304","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/trees/e408c359c3209681cab0ef1d4afa9588b34d4304"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/commits/a89a88f85fddcd56e3d6233bdeeb46502ccd320c","verification":{"payload":"tree e408c359c3209681cab0ef1d4afa9588b34d4304\nparent 05b8333cd751658e94ef9964c5762a1a6685b10a\nauthor Daniel García <dgarcia@infoblox.com> 1782943714 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782943714 -0500\n\nfeat(routing): wire apilayout URL-layout seam into shell + scaffold, fix Go-host collision (WS-019 P2+P3) (#23)\n\nBump devedge-sdk to v0.44.0 (provides the apilayout package) and use its\nURL-layout strategy seam to compose product-rest public URLs at the edge,\nresolving the WS-018 Go-host catch-all collision.\n\nShell config (P2, pkg/config):\n- spec.api.layout (default product-rest, validated via apilayout.Parse).\n- Per-domain method-1 routing: spec.api.services[] now carries {domain,\n  upstream}; each backend is routed at apilayout.<layout>.Prefix()/{domain}\n  (e.g. /api/notes) with strip-prefix, so several domains coexist on one\n  shell origin and each composes /api/{domain}/v{version}/{resource} at the\n  edge without touching proto annotations. The legacy single prefix+upstream\n  (no domain) still parses and routes as a no-domain catch-all — backward\n  compatible with the shipped method-1 shell.\n- ToRoutes builds the prefix via apilayout (never hardcodes /api) and emits\n  one strip route per domain plus the optional legacy catch-all.\n\nScaffold + Go-host fix (P3, internal/scaffold, internal/sdkscaffold, cmd/de):\n- --api-layout (default product-rest) and --domain (default = service name)\n  on `de new service` and `de project init`.\n- Emitted devedge.yaml routes the service at the app host under\n  <layout-prefix>/{domain} with stripPrefix:true INSTEAD of a host catch-all,\n  so two services (/api/foo, /api/bar) coexist under one host — collision\n  resolved and the public URL is product-rest. --host still works.\n- README/AGENTS curl examples use https://{host}/api/{domain}/v1/...\n- `de ufe new` create-default shell now sets api.layout: product-rest.\n\nTests: layout parse/default/invalid; product-rest per-domain routes\n(/api/{domain} + strip); k8s-apis /apis/{group} prefix; method-1 backward\ncompat; two-scaffolded-services-don''t-collide (both scaffolds); domain/layout\noverrides. make test (unit+integration+e2e) and make lint green. CLI reference\nregenerated for the changed help (new.md, project.md).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRY/iCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9EcQAEhcPVhhrk1w90PPDBn4MhsA\nsj3L1qUFlH5hLiQ5xjGXj2Wa4onvthI4yPvDnAglpi1wsB0TsaYgaPXfAlFWz9T5\nM6+Rb9DcXy1+h5H+UujgbnvJl0vI2638Hr2jPs50mJKCnoUVoEfwrxA1lQ7oExu6\njj5VU69uuZrt/z4+pSutTnx4S65soPLkFKrrx04TEao18AmPdny83BF4NpqHFUUu\nR/sWU3wVQSRPILWIZj5beWg2MFHibm+SHWtxW0QXNQ2XTKS7cxMAMli1DhSEw07Y\nhN8+Gz5TCe6fOz7XIO9ZiLYyaoHHkGeQ8CcVz0W46cdFxKjq/t491E/RzuFBRF3y\n2G7ztKIhpYujtSDAs1u5pjHLDGJRWlvDs0mxeAH3ACo12z8WcheiEHzl6kJSqVSO\ncUdGIyXKd+KKd2AAf4pYB5tLAYp5dgodt/eF5tZ0Zf3JXY3giQN6g3xVzAWVn7iC\n+yBfh/tmP8Yspt/TqcVkq612W+CEXPoieEG3Y69ACwBa0Hej/U1Zo7GWeI8/MjFY\no+WZ2V4969akTxedE++Rs06iilMD08dzP6q/FYJa1sJ3VfCIrzK7mK/tXEVc7N2H\n+6TPrm62dYXTVk7VAswFEoHRSH8jwMj4WSKT9IYk7OGHN8PRWtr2tbmwwNnZZAfl\nxa+k9wP442X6fGm1BGTM\n=0xYl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-01T22:08:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/w