-garcia/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/05b8333cd751658e94ef9964c5762a1a6685b10a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T21:25:49Z","email":"dgarcia@infoblox.com","name":"Daniel García"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T21:25:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ufe): de ufe new wires the shell roster + refresh CLI reference (WS-018 P-C) (#22)\n\n* feat(ufe): register `de ufe new` uFE into a shell roster (WS-018 Phase C)\n\nAfter scaffolding, `de ufe new <name>` now upserts the uFE into a\n`kind: Shell` roster so a shell picks it up — the same one-line addition\nas `de compose add`. Adding a uFE is idempotent: an existing same-id\nentry is updated in place, a new one is appended, never duplicated.\n\n- New flags: --shell (default shell.yaml), --route (default NAME),\n  --dev-port (default 4201). --shell \"\" skips roster wiring (scaffold\n  only). Existing --dir/--preset/--preset-dir are unchanged.\n- Entry = {id: <name>, route: <route>, upstream: http://127.0.0.1:<dev-port>},\n  written back through the strict schema via MarshalShell.\n- When the shell file is absent, a sensible default kind: Shell is\n  created around the one uFE (host + name derived from the uFE name,\n  shellUpstream :4200, cdn.dev.test, method-1 /api -> :8080).\n- Reports the import-map entry (id -> https://<cdn>/<route>/), the hash\n  route (#<route>), and a `de project up -f <shell>` hint.\n\nAdds Shell.UpsertUFE (config type owns the mutation). The Angular\nscaffold output is unchanged — this is purely additive roster wiring.\n\n* docs: regenerate CLI reference for path-routing + ufe roster flags\n\nregister/unregister/renew/inspect gained --path (path routing, P-A) and de ufe\nnew gained --shell/--route/--dev-port; regenerate the portal''s generated CLI\nreference so it reflects the current binary.\n\n* feat(scaffold): default edge host to app.dev.test with preset override\n\nChange the scaffold default edge host from the per-name <name>.dev.test to a\nsingle generic app.dev.test, for both the uFE shell scaffold and the Go\nservice scaffold, and add a data-driven override so a preset (the private\nInfoblox-CTO layer) can flip it to csp.dev.test without the public open core\nhardcoding a product host.\n\nuFE (de ufe new):\n- add const defaultShellHost = \"app.dev.test\"\n- create-default shell now uses host app.dev.test + metadata.name \"app\"\n  (a generic shell identity, no longer derived per-uFE); an existing\n  shell.yaml host is never rewritten\n- add ShellHost to PresetManifest + PresetShellHost() reader; when a\n  --preset-dir manifest declares a non-empty shellHost it wins over the\n  default\n\nGo service (de project init + de new service):\n- add scaffold.DefaultHost + sdkscaffold.DefaultHost = \"app.dev.test\"\n- add Host field to scaffold template data; devedge.yaml.tmpl hostname/route\n  host and the README/AGENTS curl examples now use {{.Host}}\n- add --host flag to de project init (into scaffold.Params.Host) and to\n  de new service (into sdkscaffold.Options.Host, overriding the emitted\n  devedge.yaml route host; not forwarded to devedge-sdk)\n\nTests updated for the app.dev.test default plus new override cases; CLI\nreference regenerated for new.md + project.md.","tree":{"sha":"21d16a154d9ca50186df966a4db8a3936b8cfe90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/trees/21d16a154d9ca50186df966a4db8a3936b8cfe90"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/commits/05b8333cd751658e94ef9964c5762a1a6685b10a","verification":{"payload":"tree 21d16a154d9ca50186df966a4db8a3936b8cfe90\nparent c9f31a4dba91891e0276a724dbbd8c7a047faf94\nauthor Daniel García <dgarcia@infoblox.com> 1782941149 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782941149 -0500\n\nfeat(ufe): de ufe new wires the shell roster + refresh CLI reference (WS-018 P-C) (#22)\n\n* feat(ufe): register `de ufe new` uFE into a shell roster (WS-018 Phase C)\n\nAfter scaffolding, `de ufe new <name>` now upserts the uFE into a\n`kind: Shell` roster so a shell picks it up — the same one-line addition\nas `de compose add`. Adding a uFE is idempotent: an existing same-id\nentry is updated in place, a new one is appended, never duplicated.\n\n- New flags: --shell (default shell.yaml), --route (default NAME),\n  --dev-port (default 4201). --shell \"\" skips roster wiring (scaffold\n  only). Existing --dir/--preset/--preset-dir are unchanged.\n- Entry = {id: <name>, route: <route>, upstream: http://127.0.0.1:<dev-port>},\n  written back through the strict schema via MarshalShell.\n- When the shell file is absent, a sensible default kind: Shell is\n  created around the one uFE (host + name derived from the uFE name,\n  shellUpstream :4200, cdn.dev.test, method-1 /api -> :8080).\n- Reports the import-map entry (id -> https://<cdn>/<route>/), the hash\n  route (#<route>), and a `de project up -f <shell>` hint.\n\nAdds Shell.UpsertUFE (config type owns the mutation). The Angular\nscaffold output is unchanged — this is purely additive roster wiring.\n\n* docs: regenerate CLI reference for path-routing + ufe roster flags\n\nregister/unregister/renew/inspect gained --path (path routing, P-A) and de ufe\nnew gained --shell/--route/--dev-port; regenerate the portal''s generated CLI\nreference so it reflects the current binary.\n\n* feat(scaffold): default edge host to app.dev.test with preset override\n\nChange the scaffold default edge host from the per-name <name>.dev.test to a\nsingle generic app.dev.test, for both the uFE shell scaffold and the Go\nservice scaffold, and add a data-driven override so a preset (the private\nInfoblox-CTO layer) can flip it to csp.dev.test without the public open core\nhardcoding a product host.\n\nuFE (de ufe new):\n- add const defaultShellHost = \"app.dev.test\"\n- create-default shell now uses host app.dev.test + metadata.name \"app\"\n  (a generic shell identity, no longer derived per-uFE); an existing\n  shell.yaml host is never rewritten\n- add ShellHost to PresetManifest + PresetShellHost() reader; when a\n  --preset-dir manifest declares a non-empty shellHost it wins over the\n  default\n\nGo service (de project init + de new service):\n- add scaffold.DefaultHost + sdkscaffold.DefaultHost = \"app.dev.test\"\n- add Host field to scaffold template data; devedge.yaml.tmpl hostname/route\n  host and the README/AGENTS curl examples now use {{.Host}}\n- add --host flag to de project init (into scaffold.Params.Host) and to\n  de new service (into sdkscaffold.Options.Host, overriding the emitted\n  devedge.yaml route host; not forwarded to devedge-sdk)\n\nTests updated for the app.dev.test default plus new override cases; CLI\nreference regenerated for new.md + project.md.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRYXdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiWAQAIkYsomFUT48e5OqJcN9eRNl\nw9KsoCcRSnRj/jdLVrumPr7Wf5FIxJNnDA4OPEUVIOftOtNyAcxQwab6SpPyqBRN\nenc+pvS7RkuiJVDqfhSKl5cApILCunoh2jsQh6o7GKAq3xxlLnrGMwC7yCJ2vfXd\nkbcoG1CwnecvDbCj1kAk1PJ9toWGnEoiY5JngNsqpFcRV2tfQdrGwlqDnIbOjRjd\n6fU6RMAqnV7ObtXgC13b/poO9VDcHHQmkp8QCNgoBlj987wWB46PlUzxDJyd/aeL\nmwEFFbZjeC60M43QDN2kghwGt179VILxPv56vGA6jmdCFHHJ5UbrTVu7k4rgr/yn\nk58EGbTzlQKiMZG+lPhlWRVNwGf3B96Ak4qQrlsssmEZOaElV6fygl7fumXUe7fh\nBjUeKkCGMDELtWIXWZ+hWItfXRZjjHh0SryugcGJ/UXRlqwDcT32nZ65TB9XLtZ1\nVVDIEG1KtkcFtWfu1K/XkMuzHB1pZjh2XKgud/sDbVQxzDkoLYSIHD1muOyk7R1I\ncgLQmjoVnk831iqmLD4wIAXyoHJoGgQ9UdwBfbnm/jFC7lD30tju1xWgrkCdh18f\nlmYNUouOq0jor+frIE7AK/kDbWgxmFbpwPyBtTl3N4hyHFQHznHObLwlifuzojHy\nYLH562b9LuduDiReTqWv\n=7Mq0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-01T21:25:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/infobloxopen/devedge/commit/05b8333cd751658e94ef9964c5762a1a6685b10a","node_id":"C_kwDORkaP6toAKDA1YjgzMzNjZDc1MTY1OGU5NGVmOTk2NGM1NzYyYTFhNjY4NWIxMGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/infobloxopen/devedge/commit/c9f31a4dba91891e0276a724dbbd8c7a047faf94","sha":"c9f31a4dba91891e0276a724dbbd8c7a047faf94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/c9f31a4dba91891e0276a724dbbd8c7a047faf94"}],"sha":"05b8333cd751658e94ef9964c5762a1a6685b10a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/05b8333cd751658e94ef9964c5762a1a6685b10a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/366029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/daniel-garcia","id":366029,"login":"daniel-garcia","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NjAyOQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/c9f31a4dba91891e0276a724dbbd8c7a047faf94/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T19:53:17Z","email":"dgarcia@infoblox.com","name":"Daniel García"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T19:53:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(shell): kind: Shell config for micro-frontend shell topology (WS-018 Phase B) (#21)\n\nAdd a new `kind: Shell` config resource describing a single-spa shell that\nfronts many micro-frontends, rendering it to edge routes + an import map.\n\n- pkg/config/shell.go: Shell struct + KindShell, strict ParseShell (unknown\n  fields rejected), Resource impl (Project/ToRoutes). Two API topologies:\n  method 1 (same-origin /api prefix, strip-prefixed to backend) and method 2\n  (per-service FQDNs). ToRoutes renders the shell catch-all, the API route(s),\n  and one strip-prefixed CDN route per uFE, all tagged with the project name.\n  ImportMap maps uFE id -> https://<cdn>/<route>/; HashRoutes exposes the\n  single-spa hash routes for a later phase. Validation covers required fields,\n  unique uFE id/route, method 1/2 rules, and defaults the /api prefix.\n- pkg/config/resource.go: dispatch kind: Shell through ParseShell in\n  ParseResource + add it to supportedKinds, so `de project up -f shell.yaml`\n  loads a Shell through the existing bring-up path. A Shell declares no\n  dependencies/workload, so runResourceUp''s dependency/deploy/health steps are\n  clean no-ops (type-assertion driven).\n- cmd/de/resource_up.go: carry Path/StripPrefix (and Protocol/BackendTLS) from\n  each rendered route into the register request, so path-routed routes register\n  with their prefix intact — required for the shell /api and CDN routes.\n- tests: parse (method 1/2, unknown-field, wrong-kind, missing-field matrix),\n  ToRoutes (exact Host/Path/StripPrefix/Upstream/Project per route for both\n  methods), ImportMap, HashRoutes, dispatch, round-trip.","tree":{"sha":"9222acdf3a4a4dc7f9fb7ad1baf98f3d1ebf726f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/trees/9222acdf3a4a4dc7f9fb7ad1baf98f3d1ebf726f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/commits/c9f31a4dba91891e0276a724dbbd8c7a047faf94","verification":{"payload":"tree 9222acdf3a4a4dc7f9fb7ad1baf98f3d1ebf726f\nparent 0484e12fa14771dbf8cfe8e52b36f0a77f193fd0\nauthor Daniel García <dgarcia@infoblox.com> 1782935597 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782935597 -0500\n\nfeat(shell): kind: Shell config for micro-frontend shell topology (WS-018 Phase B) (#21)\n\nAdd a new `kind: Shell` config resource describing a single-spa shell that\nfronts many micro-frontends, rendering it to edge routes + an import map.\n\n- pkg/config/shell.go: Shell struct + KindShell, strict ParseShell (unknown\n  fields rejected), Resource impl (Project/ToRoutes). Two API topologies:\n  method 1 (same-origin /api prefix, strip-prefixed to backend) and method 2\n  (per-service FQDNs). ToRoutes renders the shell catch-all, the API route(s),\n  and one strip-prefixed CDN route per uFE, all tagged with the project name.\n  ImportMap maps uFE id -> https://<cdn>/<route>/; HashRoutes exposes the\n  single-spa hash routes for a later phase. Validation covers required fields,\n  unique uFE id/route, method 1/2 rules, and defaults the /api prefix.\n- pkg/config/resource.go: dispatch kind: Shell through ParseShell in\n  ParseResource + add it to supportedKinds, so `de project up -f shell.yaml`\n  loads a Shell through the existing bring-up path. A Shell declares no\n  dependencies/workload, so runResourceUp''s dependency/deploy/health steps are\n  clean no-ops (type-assertion driven).\n- cmd/de/resource_up.go: carry Path/StripPrefix (and Protocol/BackendTLS) from\n  each rendered route into the register request, so path-routed routes register\n  with their prefix intact — required for the shell /api and CDN routes.\n- tests: parse (method 1/2, unknown-field, wrong-kind, missing-field matrix),\n  ToRoutes (exact Host/Path/StripPrefix/Upstream/Project per route for both\n  methods), ImportMap, HashRoutes, dispatch, round-trip.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRXAtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm34QAHpb01rwA05vqg9bl4jGysIZ\n2pjmifGSmPcnrzqAQQ8XBM7m/enduyRr3WpdsfOyTJ67IFuuiZZsVZNnTxV0vVYF\nSE0kjl0A4YxRZ6njNhryy2Zgsagx0BAYtWAdjLlTT2hPnwkatXVGLLq61qdv6x1J\n4GcHsJISJ0d2F6BMH66+18iMu6MqGNgSvx1FPgFYJ8jUXbuQYwDIa3pmWDvVdorA\n9hDhxeSHSmBDGE93Bu/Bq29R3kVkZyf6SE1xsP66aCfZcuJNR8LABk5JuJPMHf2b\nhE8wZs/Lde1+WN0EY0UYpiox7bei8zM7Dk+2GoGhCqqRFfeg3UmzV0gXTcAAuwH6\nPlAuiFiBeUEjb7N/l7nP7IAehebG0WuWj/T/cvstLlRXmRHDErx9gmP74oQyQtRM\nDQIA6s/DJ3g1Joz1nHRoTA5HLNxGtipz+//ye6uZlsf+ElJmf/m59LMfLH22A5sk\nf4m+xvjy5w8EulE2yiEeBcXQbC6R+MzxFCg9fgKU5lIjXF9XxqOPl1cifigXMXG9\nEfsahc2e11rB9NgtifUm+04AHupfE0mT2Kl3QlYeLdNAgy7D4i+j6hMFH2o6Kf8s\nIG+0FXqFalcpMTQeRSdA0vzzUFCXTLXhsZU4zW+zS0NcKjjQIILdRnlB8OYOWotc\n7C8jElSbb3t7hyAqnGd2\n=dULH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-01T19:53:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/infobloxopen/devedge/commit/c9f31a4dba91891e0276a724dbbd8c7a047faf94","node_id":"C_kwDORkaP6toAKGM5ZjMxYTRkYmE5MTg5MWUwMjc2YTcyNGRiYmQ4YzdhMDQ3ZmFmOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/infobloxopen/devedge/commit/0484e12fa14771dbf8cfe8e52b36f0a77f193fd0","sha":"0484e12fa14771dbf8cfe8e52b36f0a77f193fd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/0484e12fa14771dbf8cfe8e52b36f0a77f193fd0"}],"sha":"c9f31a4dba91891e0276a724dbbd8c7a047faf94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/c9f31a4dba91891e0276a724dbbd8c7a047faf94"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/366029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/daniel-garcia","id":366029,"login":"daniel-garcia","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NjAyOQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/0484e12fa14771dbf8cfe8e52b36f0a77f193fd0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T19:35:04Z","email":"dgarcia@infoblox.com","name":"Daniel García"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T19:35:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(routing): path-prefix routing on the local edge (WS-018 Phase A) (#20)\n\nLet one host fan out to multiple upstreams distinguished by URL path prefix,\nso the in-process reverse proxy can serve the single-origin micro-frontend\nshell topology (e.g. app.dev.test/ -> shell, app.dev.test/api/... -> backend).\nEmpty path + strip-prefix off preserves today''s exact one-host/one-route\nbehavior; all changes are backward compatible.\n\nChanges:\n- types.Route: add optional Path (URL path prefix; \"\" = host catch-all) and\n  StripPrefix (trim Path before forwarding, for gateways serving /v1 behind\n  /api).\n- registry: store routes under a two-level (host, path) map. Register conflict\n  and create/renew are now keyed by (host, path) — first-writer-wins per path;\n  a new path under an existing host is additive. Lookup(host, reqPath) returns\n  the longest-prefix match, with a path-less route as the catch-all; a\n  host-only lookup defaults reqPath to \"/\" (keeps TCP SNI dispatch and\n  `de inspect HOST` working). Deregister(host) removes ALL routes for a host;\n  Deregister(host, path) removes just one. DeregisterProject, List, Sweep, and\n  onChange events all iterate the new model.\n- proxy handler(): look up by Lookup(host, r.URL.Path); when the matched route\n  has StripPrefix, trim Path from req.URL.Path before forwarding (empty result\n  guarded to \"/\"). 502 unchanged when the host has no route.\n- daemon API: RegisterRequest carries path/strip_prefix; GET and DELETE\n  /v1/routes/{host} accept an optional ?path= to target one (host, path)\n  route.\n- client: Lookup/Deregister take an optional path (thread ?path=).\n- CLI: `de register` gains --path and --strip-prefix; `de unregister`,\n  `de renew`, `de inspect` gain --path (renew now also re-registers\n  protocol/backend-tls, previously dropped).\n- config: RouteEntry accepts path:/stripPrefix:; threaded through Project,\n  Service, and Composition ToRoutes.\n- render/traefik: a route with Path renders Host(`h`) && PathPrefix(`p`) at a\n  priority above the bare-Host catch-all, plus a stripPrefix middleware when\n  set. Path-less routes render exactly as before. Config filenames/router\n  names fold in a sanitized path so several routes per host no longer collide.\n\nTests:\n- registry: longest-prefix selection (/, /api, /api/v1), path-less catch-all,\n  boundary (/apiary not under /api), host-only default-to-root, per-(host,path)\n  conflict vs additive, deregister host-all vs single-path, DeregisterProject\n  multi-path.\n- proxy (httptest): two upstreams under one host (/ -> A, /api -> B), correct\n  routing, StripPrefix trims /api/x -> /x, non-strip preserves full path, 502\n  on unrouted host, backward-compat full-path passthrough.\n- config: project + service (strict decoder) parse and ToRoutes round-trip for\n  path/stripPrefix.\n- daemon: register two routes on one host, GET/DELETE ?path= semantics.\n- render: Host && PathPrefix + priority + stripPrefix middleware; path-less\n  unchanged; SyncAll writes distinct files per (host, path).\n\nVerification:\n- `make test` (go test ./...): all packages green.\n- `make lint` (go vet ./...): clean.\n\nFull real-edge e2e was NOT run in this sandbox: it needs the daemon bound on\n127.0.0.2:443 with the mkcert CA (privileged port + loopback alias + sudo),\nwhich the sandbox cannot provide. The proxy-level httptest above is the\nautomated proof. Manual real-edge verification (run on a machine with\n`de install` + `de start` done):\n  1. de register app.dev.test http://127.0.0.1:3000            # shell (catch-all)\n  2. de register app.dev.test http://127.0.0.1:8080 --path /api --strip-prefix\n  3. curl -s https://app.dev.test/            -> reaches :3000, path \"/\"\n  4. curl -s https://app.dev.test/api/hello   -> reaches :8080, path \"/hello\"\n  5. de inspect app.dev.test --path /api      -> shows path=/api strip=true\n  6. de unregister app.dev.test --path /api   -> only /api removed; / still routes\n  7. de unregister app.dev.test               -> host cleared","tree":{"sha":"dd0e7db06596282c23c49177e8471941e19fc1fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/trees/dd0e7db06596282c23c49177e8471941e19fc1fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/commits/0484e12fa14771dbf8cfe8e52b36f0a77f193fd0","verification":{"payload":"tree dd0e7db06596282c23c49177e8471941e19fc1fb\nparent 16afde0bc6290c5d03b7eda8ace52c699f7fa9c5\nauthor Daniel García <dgarcia@infoblox.com> 1782934504 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782934504 -0500\n\nfeat(routing): path-prefix routing on the local edge (WS-018 Phase A) (#20)\n\nLet one host fan out to multiple upstreams distinguished by URL path prefix,\nso the in-process reverse proxy can serve the single-origin micro-frontend\nshell topology (e.g. app.dev.test/ -> shell, app.dev.test/api/... -> backend).\nEmpty path + strip-prefix off preserves today''s exact one-host/one-route\nbehavior; all changes are backward compatible.\n\nChanges:\n- types.Route: add optional Path (URL path prefix; \"\" = host catch-all) and\n  StripPrefix (trim Path before forwarding, for gateways serving /v1 behind\n  /api).\n- registry: store routes under a two-level (host, path) map. Register conflict\n  and create/renew are now keyed by (host, path) — first-writer-wins per path;\n  a new path under an existing host is additive. Lookup(host, reqPath) returns\n  the longest-prefix match, with a path-less route as the catch-all; a\n  host-only lookup defaults reqPath to \"/\" (keeps TCP SNI dispatch and\n  `de inspect HOST` working). Deregister(host) removes ALL routes for a host;\n  Deregister(host, path) removes just one. DeregisterProject, List, Sweep, and\n  onChange events all iterate the new model.\n- proxy handler(): look up by Lookup(host, r.URL.Path); when the matched route\n  has StripPrefix, trim Path from req.URL.Path before forwarding (empty result\n  guarded to \"/\"). 502 unchanged when the host has no route.\n- daemon API: RegisterRequest carries path/strip_prefix; GET and DELETE\n  /v1/routes/{host} accept an optional ?path= to target one (host, path)\n  route.\n- client: Lookup/Deregister take an optional path (thread ?path=).\n- CLI: `de register` gains --path and --strip-prefix; `de unregister`,\n  `de renew`, `de inspect` gain --path (renew now also re-registers\n  protocol/backend-tls, previously dropped).\n- config: RouteEntry accepts path:/stripPrefix:; threaded through Project,\n  Service, and Composition ToRoutes.\n- render/traefik: a route with Path renders Host(`h`) && PathPrefix(`p`) at a\n  priority above the bare-Host catch-all, plus a stripPrefix middleware when\n  set. Path-less routes render exactly as before. Config filenames/router\n  names fold in a sanitized path so several routes per host no longer collide.\n\nTests:\n- registry: longest-prefix selection (/, /api, /api/v1), path-less catch-all,\n  boundary (/apiary not under /api), host-only default-to-root, per-(host,path)\n  conflict vs additive, deregister host-all vs single-path, DeregisterProject\n  multi-path.\n- proxy (httptest): two upstreams under one host (/ -> A, /api -> B), correct\n  routing, StripPrefix trims /api/x -> /x, non-strip preserves full path, 502\n  on unrouted host, backward-compat full-path passthrough.\n- config: project + service (strict decoder) parse and ToRoutes round-trip for\n  path/stripPrefix.\n- daemon: register two routes on one host, GET/DELETE ?path= semantics.\n- render: Host && PathPrefix + priority + stripPrefix middleware; path-less\n  unchanged; SyncAll writes distinct files per (host, path).\n\nVerification:\n- `make test` (go test ./...): all packages green.\n- `make lint` (go vet ./...): clean.\n\nFull real-edge e2e was NOT run in this sandbox: it needs the daemon bound on\n127.0.0.2:443 with the mkcert CA (privileged port + loopback alias + sudo),\nwhich the sandbox cannot provide. The proxy-level httptest above is the\nautomated proof. Manual real-edge verification (run on a machine with\n`de install` + `de start` done):\n  1. de register app.dev.test http://127.0.0.1:3000            # shell (catch-all)\n  2. de register app.dev.test http://127.0.0.1:8080 --path /api --strip-prefix\n  3. curl -s https://app.dev.test/            -> reaches :3000, path \"/\"\n  4. curl -s https://app.dev.test/api/hello   -> reaches :8080, path \"/hello\"\n  5. de inspect app.dev.test --path /api      -> shows path=/api strip=true\n  6. de unregister app.dev.test --path /api   -> only /api removed; / still routes\n  7. de unregister app.dev.test               -> host cleared","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRWvoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3BgQAB0lFXWZBEh/MAahqmQNto5x\n5MqEp2F0YQTQth3MY7yCaO3Cw+9/E7lsK+4vINEbPIm+Wf8hzLN1tNCsl5ynx4pg\nIzB4pNp5q5oQx6PRfYUYQEmKFh4vjfmDSApPEL7eIo1pdR1UfRIFBM3InGGij522\nC4Eh0t8Gou27S1iLO8ZIQx115EvqBpQ6uFaR5hYBIXU1aYkw9EyhzMvbl3KlObm3\nOupv3BQ3GR0egGki+DQPxD+SGtfm/dT3I6oTUN785OCa/mo3ThaJknZukOWrwH1d\nwWAeLU8CcrMS94gQBRY08jUnjJG6xYJS3xBBr0qq6GYqqQw6AULrQIfwxce5RDHv\n+Dckx3a3vG09p8o9b1STIpbiqfL8bv37B9yA5YRTUlEFyiixUtLB4jWTcHEuUy+d\nr9LjBbIU0PBYpZOuruxOE85u9+FO7KW2iO1evDlu+iPNG3c4GPbpScSpCZSqODQF\nKP4YTxxdMVdJsm7hvd0Nlikztmp63+rxUwZpl5RNlzLHCyII0DwvFVDJoTkfU7b6\nyktwgEI/rAqd8h3Q+aw1lBsPokouUDjM9UoUtA3D1sn70BfdspOQ15q5YTnEiJp6\nQh