om/users/daniel-garcia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/commits/577a649cc766f45066eafbb9406da31782dfe0c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T22:03:16Z","email":"dgarcia@infoblox.com","name":"Daniel Garcia"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T22:03:16Z","email":"dgarcia@infoblox.com","name":"Daniel Garcia"},"message":"Fix migrations path resolution for relative -f (daemon-side ENOENT)\n\nresolveMigrationPath joined against filepath.Dir(-f), which is \".\" for the\ndefault -f devedge.yaml — the path validated CLI-side (cwd = project) and\nthen failed inside the daemon (different cwd): open db/migrations: no such\nfile or directory. Anchor the project dir with filepath.Abs before joining;\nthe resolved path crosses the CLI->daemon process boundary and must be\nabsolute. Found by the 007 onboarding walk-through human run (friction #6);\nregression test pins Migrations(\".\") returning an absolute dir.","tree":{"sha":"0b57c8e92b05eb0df776a01d4488a249ca251d3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/trees/0b57c8e92b05eb0df776a01d4488a249ca251d3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infobloxopen/devedge/git/commits/577a649cc766f45066eafbb9406da31782dfe0c6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/366029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-garcia/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/daniel-garcia","id