s/HeadySystems/Heady-AI/commits/8a92204086629e513523c9c7295b206f0af4fada"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250789142?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeadyConnection/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeadyConnection/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeadyConnection/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeadyConnection/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/HeadyConnection","id":250789142,"login":"HeadyConnection","node_id":"U_kgDODvK9Fg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeadyConnection/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeadyConnection/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeadyConnection/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeadyConnection/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeadyConnection/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeadyConnection","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeadySystems/Heady-AI/commits/5a19d0d761dce96f63864cabb2d32b3d2777ed5d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T17:38:51Z","email":"eric@headysystems.com","name":"Eric Haywood"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T17:38:51Z","email":"eric@headysystems.com","name":"Eric Haywood"},"message":"fix(db): make the 0001→0006 migration chain apply on Neon (0003/0004 portability)\n\nA full chain apply on a fresh Neon database (confirmed: production root is empty —\nno roles beyond neondb_owner, no journal) halted before reaching the 990 migrations.\nTwo behavior-preserving fixes, both proven live on a COW branch off root:\n\n- 0003_data_api_least_privilege: guard the `authenticated` REVOKEs with\n  `IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_roles WHERE rolname=''authenticated'')` — the SAME\n  idiom 0004 already uses for its own authenticated REVOKEs. Unguarded, it threw\n  \"role authenticated does not exist\" on any DB without the Neon Data-API role.\n  No-op when the role is absent; full lockdown when present (deploy-ordering:\n  enable the Data API BEFORE migrating so it binds).\n\n- 0004_approval_control_plane: REMOVE the redundant `ALTER ROLE heady_approval_api\n  WITH ... NOSUPERUSER NOBYPASSRLS`. `CREATE ROLE ... NOLOGIN` already yields those\n  attributes as defaults; setting SUPERUSER/BYPASSRLS attributes requires a PG\n  superuser, which Neon never grants neondb_owner → \"permission denied to alter\n  role\" halted the ENTIRE chain on every Neon endpoint. Role posture unchanged.\n\nAPPROVAL OWNER: 0004''s file bytes changed, so its genesis migration_sha256\n(computed dynamically by packages/approvals/bin/prepare-genesis-manifest.mjs) will\ndiffer — regenerate the genesis manifest before the next approval bootstrap. No\npinned hash exists in source; runtime bootstrap integrity is owned by the approval\nwork.\n\nVerified: full 0001→0006 applies GREEN on a fresh Neon branch (990 hybrid +\nheady_approval schema live); migrate.test.mjs 19/19; governance + coherence +\nturbo 86/86 green. Does NOT deploy to root (still gated on a root credential reset).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"846a1d3d7f710bb960635faa6840913c77027be6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeadySystems/Heady-AI/git/trees/846a1d3d7f710bb960635faa6840913c77027be6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeadySystems/Heady-AI/git/commits/5a19d0d761dce96f63864cabb2d32b3d2777ed5d","verification":{"payload":"tree 846a1d3d7f710bb960635faa6840913c77027be6\nparent 22f48a26e3b91b094cfe92dd8e8edc211d1c13aa\nauthor Eric Haywood <eric@headysystems.com> 1785346731 -0600\ncommitter Eric Haywood <eric@headysystems.com> 1785346731 -0600\n\nfix(db): make the 0001→0006 migration chain apply on Neon (0003/0004 portability)\n\nA full chain apply on a fresh Neon database (confirmed: production root is empty —\nno roles beyond neondb_owner, no journal) halted before reaching the 990 migrations.\nTwo behavior-preserving fixes, both proven live on a COW branch off root:\n\n- 0003_data_api_least_privilege: guard the `authenticated` REVOKEs with\n  `IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_roles WHERE rolname=''authenticated'')` — the SAME\n  idiom 0004 already uses for its own authenticated REVOKEs. Unguarded, it threw\n  \"role authenticated does not exist\" on any DB without the Neon Data-API role.\n  No-op when the role is absent; full lockdown when present (deploy-ordering:\n  enable the Data API BEFORE migrating so it binds).\n\n- 0004_approval_control_plane: REMOVE the redundant `ALTER ROLE heady_approval_api\n  WITH ... NOSUPERUSER NOBYPASSRLS`. `CREATE ROLE ... NOLOGIN` already yields those\n  attributes as defaults; setting SUPERUSER/BYPASSRLS attributes requires a PG\n  superuser, which Neon never grants neondb_owner → \"permission denied to alter\n  role\" halted the ENTIRE chain on every Neon endpoint. Role posture unchanged.\n\nAPPROVAL OWNER: 0004''s file bytes changed, so its genesis migration_sha256\n(computed dynamically by packages/approvals/bin/prepare-genesis-manifest.mjs) will\ndiffer — regenerate the genesis manifest before the next approval bootstrap. No\npinned hash exists in source; runtime bootstrap integrity is owned by the approval\nwork.\n\nVerified: full 0001→0006 applies GREEN on a fresh Neon branch (990 hybrid +\nheady_approval schema live); migrate.test.mjs 19/19; governance + coherence +\nturbo 86/86 green. Does NOT deploy to root (still gated on a root credential reset).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"unverified_email","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQQQULWecpbEbCbd+V2n0hCLs8YQHAUCamo6qwAKCRCn0hCLs8YQ\nHC3vAP4i9XUkTfrX8keE9QfWeFeBNPJ6qvgZaegH7fstg8MJ+gEAnixb/LpiAFDm\nM7S5lzgrWOwO9mtkgrUvkU0JWPoajwI=\n=9Eg8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avata