ns_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeadyConnection/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeadyConnection","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeadySystems/Heady-AI/commits/0976d9376c5e7a31929576744a4f14a362c67117/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T14:18:27Z","email":"eric@headysystems.com","name":"Eric Haywood"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T14:18:27Z","email":"eric@headysystems.com","name":"Eric Haywood"},"message":"feat(laws): #11 merkle-trigger enforced — the trigger was already built\n\nInvestigation for \"the next invariant leg\" found ADR-0023''s authoritative\nfile-change trigger ALREADY REAL: packages/embedding/src/corpus.mjs (sha256\nbinary Merkle, path-bound leaves, ledger-authoritative planning with backfill\nsemantics, 10 corpus tests) consumed by tooling/embed-corpus phase 3. Live\ndry-run proof over the 689-file gate-passed corpus: incremental diff 271\nadded / 105 changed / 313 unchanged / 21 removed, 313 backfill jobs correctly\ndetected (a prior run advanced the index with no embedder bound — the\nledger-authority design catching exactly its target failure).\n\nSo the leg is enforcement, not construction: coherence LAW11-* (pure\ncheckMerkleTrigger in packages-law.mjs) asserts the embed orchestrator\nderives from planCorpusEmbedding AND zero Postgres-CDC machinery\n(pg-logical-replication/wal2json/pgoutput/START_REPLICATION/CREATE\nPUBLICATION) inside the file-index path (packages/embedding, embed-corpus,\nawareness). laws.json #11 → enforced. Tamper-proven: de-wiring the planner\nimport trips 0→1 contradictions; the first tamper round exposed a substring\nmatch (planCorpusEmbeddingX passed) — fixed with word boundaries before\nshipping. Advisory remainder is now #7 redis-namespace alone.\n\nGates: 10/10 green · turbo 79/79 · coherence tests 23/23 · embedding 18/18.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e8af5612e5d8