eceived_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/ra-skills/commits/267c0746974af712cc6dcab18c394eaf72c19e66/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T17:05:57Z","email":"gabriel.borg93@gmail.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T17:05:57Z","email":"gabriel.borg93@gmail.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(skills): apply writing-great-skills audit fixes across the Python/build stack\n\n- dagger, writing-python, python-infrastructure, fastapi (+otel): fix broken and\n  contradictory code samples (slowapi async+redis:// wiring, verify_password tuple\n  truth-test, module-level engine, PEP 695 ModelType leftovers, nonexistent\n  ctx.new_uuid(), SecretStr gotcha, BuildLocal arity, +default= pragma form),\n  resolve cross-skill ownership (rate limiting -> fastapi, OTel generics ->\n  otel, sampling in Collector, deployment.environment.name), prune description\n  context load, and dedupe repeated rules to single-source-of-truth pointers\n- README: reference mattpocock/skills in §4 (vendor-CLI, per-skill picker) and\n  adopt writing-great-skills as the skill-authoring standard (Contributing)\n- sync marketplace.json descriptions; regenerate agents/AGENTS.md + README table","tree":{"sha":"e55dfd2351c26a833541624bf714a76f373c363f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/ra-skills/git/trees/e55dfd2351c26a833541624bf714a76f373c363f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/ra-skills/git/commits/267c0746974af712cc6dcab18c394eaf72c19e66","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at