//api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/ra-skills/commits/34318d92cf612ef821c752a504bd9886a1f6e506/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-25T13:00:05Z","email":"gabriel.borg93@gmail.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-25T13:00:05Z","email":"gabriel.borg93@gmail.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(architecture-diagram): harden template edit-comment against tag-anchored string surgery\n\nThe <head> \"EDIT THESE THINGS\" comment literally contained <title>/<h1>/<header>,\nwhich sit before the real elements. Any tag-anchored automation (a build script''s\ntext.index(\"<header>\"), a regex <header>...</header>, or an Edit anchored on\n<header>) matched the comment first and sliced out the entire <style> block,\nproducing an unstyled, dead page.\n\n- template.html: reword line 13 to prose with no bare tag literals, so\n  index(\"<header>\")/index(\"<h1>\") now resolve to the real elements.\n- SKILL.md: add a Common-pitfalls bullet — don''t anchor scripted edits on bare\n  tag names (two <style> blocks exist; title/header text recurs); anchor on the\n  {{...}} placeholders or class selectors instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f4d6ce1ecd6acb94fe4a1d41c9e5c07f81065e41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/ra-skills/git/trees/f4d6ce1ecd6acb94fe4a1d41c9e5c07f81065e41"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/ra-skills/git/commits/34318d92cf612ef821c752a504bd9886a1f6e506","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"ht